    "case_for": "B045 identifies a compact, foundational contribution with lasting reach across statistical physics and quantum field theory. Conformal field theory turned symmetry into a rigorous route to exact, universal results for two-dimensional critical phenomena. Its central results have been extensively developed and applied, giving the case both conceptual depth and maturity. The credited trio is appropriate for this tightly connected contribution.",
    "case_against": "The scope needs historical discipline: important developments in conformal symmetry preceded this work, and an overly broad citation could claim more than the trio established. The prize should recognize the framework's decisive role in two-dimensional critical phenomena without implying sole authorship of conformal methods or every later application.",
    "responses": [
