        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson argues that the Aharonov–Bohm and Berry phases are distinct but complementary insights whose shared citation must make their separate contributions clear.",
        "response": "I agree that joining distinct discoveries can blur attribution. That concern also applies to B027, but B045 is more naturally bounded as one framework and a connected body of foundational work. Its citation should still state the specific achievement in two-dimensional critical phenomena and acknowledge the historical development of conformal symmetry."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll finds cavity optomechanics experimentally substantial but broad and cumulative, with no uniquely bounded prize-sized result or contributor set.",
        "response": "That is a real concern for B003. B045 has a more focused intellectual center: a framework enabling exact, universal results in two-dimensional critical phenomena, with a foundational trio already identified. Its later influence is broad, but the citation can remain tied to that specific advance."
      }
    ],
